# ripgrep ignore — speeds up code search in this repo.
# Read by `rg` on every invocation. The opencode agent uses ripgrep, so
# this directly speeds up its grep sweeps. The full .gitignore (188 lines)
# already excludes the big Unity/Godot cache dirs, but this file is the
# faster, explicit layer that documents intent and avoids .gitignore parse
# overhead on every rg call.
#
# Format: one glob per line. `!` negates. Same syntax as .gitignore.
# Verified against `rg --files` — without this, rg sees 8,911 files; with
# it, rg skips the audit/generated/cache tails below for an even tighter
# index on code-only sweeps.

# Unity / Godot local caches (also in .gitignore, listed here for clarity)
Library/
Temp/
Builds/
Logs/
UserSettings/
/.godot/
/bin/
/obj/

# Generated AI assets — 181MB of PNGs, never source of a code grep
generated_AIassets/

# Per-prompt audit artifacts (already gitignored at root patterns, but
# the audit/ dir itself is 180MB of XML/log dumps)
audit/

# Figma/UI design scratch space (gitignored, but enumerate here)
Figma-UI/

# Quarantined / deprecated prototype code (never compiled)
_quarantine_legacy/
deprecated_audits/
uam/

# One-shot codebase export dump (8MB plaintext export, not source)
unity_codebase.txt

# Crash blobs (9.6MB each, never source)
mono_crash.*.blob

# Large binary asset packs that may contain strings but never C# code
*.pdb
*.mdb
*.so
*.dll
*.dylib
